  "identifier": "fastslide",
  "name": "FastSlide",
  "description": "High-performance C++20 library for reading whole slide images (WSI) in digital pathology, with first-class Python bindings. Thread-safe, AI/ML-native design with PyTorch DataLoader compatibility for multi-worker loading. Supports 11+ formats: SVS, QPTIFF, OME-TIFF, OME.ZARR, MRXS, iSyntax, Philips TIFF, CZI (Zeiss), Ventana (BIF), Olympus VSI, and generic TIFF. Supports multi-dimensional images (channels, focal planes Z, time points T) and multiple scenes per file (CZI scenes, Olympus VSI regions). Level-native coordinate system. Installable via pip. Developed by George Yiasemis, Rolf Harkes, and Jonas Teuwen at the Netherlands Cancer Institute AI division (NKI-AI). Apache-2.0, v0.7.0, 38 stars.",
