  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Modern high-performance WSI reader from the Netherlands Cancer Institute AI division — designed specifically for AI/ML pathology workflows where OpenSlide's single-threaded design is a bottleneck. C++20 core with Python bindings, PyTorch DataLoader compatible, thread-safe, supports 11+ formats including iSyntax (Philips) and CZI (Zeiss) which OpenSlide does not cover. Apache-2.0. Assess rather than Adopt: pre-1.0 (v0.7.0), 38 GitHub stars, and no peer-reviewed paper yet. OpenSlide (Adopt in MACH) remains the production standard; FastSlide is the emerging alternative for teams hitting performance limits or needing broader format coverage. Assess for new AI/ML pathology pipelines where multi-worker loading and multi-dimensional image support are requirements.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-04",
